---
import Slide from '../ui/Slide.astro';
import Callout from '../ui/Callout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../ui/CodeBlock.astro';
import Pill from '../ui/Pill.astro';
---

<Slide
  id="s15b-layer-infra-commands"
  chapter="Layers"
  title="Infrastructure Layer — Commands"
  notes="External path first: dig and curl prove what users see. Node health cluster-wide before pod logs. Myth: one working kubectl path hides broken worker networking or load balancers."
>
  <div class="stagger flex flex-col gap-6">
    <section>
      <h3 class="mb-3 font-display text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-deck-cyan">Typical commands</h3>
      <CodeBlock
        lang="bash"
        caption="External + cluster sanity"
        code={`# External path
dig +short api.example.com
curl -vI https://app.example.com

# Cluster-wide node health
kubectl get nodes -o wide
kubectl get events -A --field-selector type=Warning | tail -20`}
      />
    </section>

    <Callout type="myth">
      If <code class="text-deck-cyan/90">kubectl</code> works, infrastructure is fine. One working admin path hides broken worker networking, DNS, or load balancers.
    </Callout>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 border-t border-deck-border/60 pt-4">
      <Pill tone="amber">Decision hint</Pill>
      <span class="text-lg text-deck-muted">Cluster-wide + external impact → verify region, DNS, and LB before diving into pod logs.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</Slide>
